      "message": "Hi Kelvin, would you be OK with dropping this patch? As far as I can tell it doesn\u0027t change anything for 64-bit tasks: a 4KB process\u0027s `mm-\u003etask_size` is still `TASK_SIZE_64` (`setup_new_exec()` sets it from arm64\u0027s own `TASK_SIZE`, since `fs/exec.c` doesn\u0027t include `\u003clinux/p3s_user_pages.h\u003e`), and `TASK_SIZE_4KB` only feeds `mm_task_size()`. So `ctx-\u003emm-\u003etask_size` and `current-\u003emm-\u003etask_size` are the same for any 64-bit handler, and the `-EINVAL` that the commit message describes can\u0027t happen. Only AArch32 tasks, which P3S doesn\u0027t support, would see a difference. Will asked to squash it into aosp/4312528, and I\u0027ve replied there with the details.",
